        "3. **Ignoring positional information.**  Self-attention alone is permutation equivariant; language requires order.\n",
        "4. **Using the wrong mask orientation.**  In causal attention, query position $i$ may attend to key position $j$ only when $j\\le i$.\n",
        "5. **Confusing token type and token position.**  The same word appearing twice can have two different contextual embeddings.\n",
        "6. **Overlooking quadratic cost.**  Full attention stores a $T\\times T$ matrix for each head.\n",
